    "message": {
     "content": "### The Bottom Line\n**Yes, from a compensation standpoint, you should take this offer.**\n\nA **$200,000 sign-on bonus** at Google L6 is at the absolute top of their discretionary exception band. They matched your base salary and effectively paid you cash upfront for your unvested Meta RSUs *on top* of Google\u2019s standard front-loaded equity. \n\nNegotiation has reached its limit; pushing further risks goodwill.\n\n---\n\n### The Financial Breakdown\n\nBecause Google front-loads equity grants (**33% / 33% / 22% / 12%**), your total compensation over the next two years is exceptionally high:\n\n| Component | Year 1 | Year 2 | Year 3 (Base + Target) | Year 4 (Base + Target) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 | $240,000 |\n| **Target Bonus (20%)** | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 | $48,000 |\n| **GSU Equity** | $356,400 (33%) | $356,400 (33%) | $237,600 (22%) | $129,600 (12%) |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $200,000 | $0 | $0 | $0 |\n| **Estimated Total Comp** | **~$844,400** | **~$644,400** | **~$525,600\\*** | **~$417,600\\*** |\n\n*\\*Years 3 and 4 do not include annual performance refreshers, which will stack on top of these numbers.*\n\n#### Comparison vs. Staying at Meta:\n* **2-Year Comparison:** You will make **~$1.49M at Google** vs. **~$1.05M at Meta**. That is a **~$440,000+ net gain** in your first 24 months.\n* **4-Year Cumulative:** Even if you received *zero* equity refreshers at Google, your 4-year total comp would be **~$2.43M** (averaging ~$608k/yr), beating your current Meta run-rate of ~$2.1M over the same period.\n\n---\n\n### Key Details to Confirm Before Signing\n\n1. **Sign-On Bonus Terms:**\n   * **Disbursement:** Verify whether the $200k is paid out in a single lump sum in your first 1\u20132 paychecks or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k / $100k).\n   * **Clawback:** Google standard sign-on clawbacks are typically 12 months (pro-rated monthly if you leave before 1 year). Ensure it is not a 24-month clawback.\n2. **Team & Scope:**\n   * At Google, team placement and your direct L7+ manager dictate your day-to-day experience and promotion velocity far more than level bands. Ensure you are aligned with the San Francisco team's roadmap and leadership before accepting.\n3. **Culture Shift (Meta vs. Google PM):**\n   * **Meta PMs** generally operate with high top-down urgency, quantitative metric ownership, and rapid shipping velocity.\n   * **Google PMs** typically operate in a more consensus-driven, engineering-centric culture where stakeholder alignment across cross-functional orgs takes more time. Make sure this shift aligns with your working style.\n\n---\n\n### What About a Meta Counter-Offer?\n\nIf you are genuinely torn because you love Meta, you can bring this offer to your VP/HR to explore a retention package. Meta often matches or issues retention refreshers to defend senior talent against Google. \n\nHowever, given that Google has offered you **~$844k for Year 1**, Meta would need to issue a significant off-cycle grant to match that immediate liquidity. If you do explore a counter-offer, be prepared to accept Google immediately if Meta declines to match.",
